# SYNOPSIS

```text
userboot.next=bin/launcher launcher.until=sd-test
```

# DESCRIPTION

sd-test is the last service of the SD image, `bootfs-sdhci-test.img`, which holds devmgr(8) with its drivers and the services its manifest mounts.
The boot-sdhci test boots it in QEMU with an SD card in a version 3 sdhci-pci host (`tools/qemu.sh --sd`), a 64 MiB card that vx-disk(1) makes with a taisce partition, anew each run.
The launcher runs until sd-test ends and exits with its code (launcher(8)).

It waits up to 30 seconds for sdhci(3) to bring the card up or fail, and prints the driver's `status`, a line each, `sd-test: sdhci: <line>`.
It checks that the card came up, that `/dev/sdM0/ctl` answers with the disk's geometry and the card's `taisce` partition, read from its GPT, and prints that `ctl`.
Then it writes 160 KiB of random bytes to `/dev/sdM0/data` 64 KiB in, past the partition table, so the driver takes two pieces of its 128 KiB buffer, and checks that they read back the same; and that 100 bytes read at an offset no sector starts at are the bytes written there.
A line for each check is `sd-test: ok:` or `sd-test: FAILED:` and what it checks; its last line is `sd-test: passed` or `sd-test: <n> failed`.
It exits 0 if every check passed.

# FILES

: `build/<arch>/esp-sdhci-test`
